Z||000000||snafus87||12-11-2001||11:19 PM||||Ok, here is the deal...<P>I just replaced the alternator on my car tonight with no problems(other than a bolt breaking off...nbd)<P>I took it for a spin to make sure everything was in working order.  While I was on my drive, everything seemed fine for the first 20 minutes of the trip.  However, I pulled into a gas station to turn around and head home and when I pulled back out to get up to speed, the idiot light came on.  I didn't notice any load loss for voltage...I turned on my a/c, fog lamps, blower motor on high, hit the brakes to turn on the brake lights, and turned on the 4 ways, and not even the slightest dimming of lights anywhere or the fan slowing down at all...everything seems fine, except the dummy light for the alternator is on now...<P>Any ideas?  I need to get this remedied asap, as I have no other car to drive at the moment...<P>HELP!!!<P>------------------<BR>JT Krupa<BR>85 GT<BR>(fastback conversion)<BR>180+ K miles<BR>Lehighton, PA||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierohoho||12-12-2001||05:01 AM||||It is possible the new alt. is bad.<P>I just put a new one in my wifes Tempo and it was bad.<P>A good idea is to have the parts store bench check your new one and if it's bad they can replace it but have them check the replacement before you leave to make sure it's good.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-12-2001||05:20 AM||||Yep, the new alternator is bad, even if it is charging.  It most likely has a bad diode to turn the light on and still charge.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||dcaprio||12-13-2001||07:10 AM||||Yes the alternater was bad ( overcharging ). Snafas and I changed it for the 2nd time in 2 days. Very easy doing it the 2nd time. Believe it or not but next week we have to change another alternator on the 86 Gt i just bought. We should be very good at it after that||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pyric||12-13-2001||07:40 AM||||Is it a direct replacement?  If you put in a higher output alternator the same thing can happen, even if it is working fine.  <P>But if it is OEM I agree that it's probably not all working right.  I had one work for 3 months and then die.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>That lifetime warranty thing on rebuilt alternators rocks!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronegS.jpg">   <P><BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
